: Grade 3\n Grade 8\n 2020-2021: Grade 4\n 2019-2020: Grade 4\n Grade 10\n 2020-2021 Grade 5\n 2019-2020: Grade 5\n Grade 11\n 2020-2021: Grade 6 12","Examining cohort growth trends over time\n• Taking account of what grades the students were in when the\n pandemic happened, we can examine both how this cohort grew\n over time as well as how the system “adapted” as they increased\n from grade to grade.\n• For example, one caution expressed following the pandemic was\n that students whose early literacy instruction was severely\n disrupted could face increased risk of downstream academic\n adversity due to inadequate foundational skills.\n• We consider, for example, the students currently in Grade 7 who\n were in Grade 2 (spring 2020) and Grade 3 (2020-2021 academic\n year).\n\n 13","ELA Grade 4 2023, 2024 2025\n Student Growth Percentile Goodness−of−Fit Descriptives Student Growth Percentile Goodness−of−Fit Descriptives Student Growth Percentile Goodness−of−Fit Descriptives\n 2023 English Language Arts SGP, Grade 4 (N = 20,037) 2024 English Language Arts SGP, Grade 4 (N = 20,233) 2025 English Language Arts SGP, Grade 4 (N = 19,819)\n\n SGP Deciles by Prior Achievement Level (ELA) SGP Deciles by Prior Achievement Level (ELA) SGP Deciles by Prior Achievement Level (ELA)\n Advanced (15.9%)\n Advanced (21.1%) Advanced (17.9%)\n\n Prior Achievement Level Prior Achievement Level Prior Achievement Level\n Proficient (16.2%) Proficient (14.6%)\n Proficient (15.3%)\n\n Near Proficient (41.1%)\n Near Proficient (37.5%) Near Proficient (39.2%)\n\n Novice (26.9%) Novice (26%) Novice (28.3%)\n\n 1 10 20 30 40 50 60 70 80 90 99 1 10 20 30 40 50 60 70 80 90 99 1 10 20 30 40 50 60 70 80 90 99\n Median Student Growth Percentile Median Student Growth Percentile Median Student Growth Percentile\n\n Ceiling / Floor Effects Test Ceiling / Floor Effects Test Ceiling / Floor Effects Test\n Student Growth Percentile Range Student Growth Percentile Range Student Growth Percentile Range\n\n 